\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Server Overview
\par \plain\fs24 The Leo-32 Server is the central controller of the microscope. It co-ordinates requests for data and control actions from other applications which it routes to low level control modules and also notifies all relevant applications of changes in the microscope.
\par 
\par The server must therefore remain active whenever the microscope is in use.
\par 
\par The server is also responsible for performing the log on  function when an interface application is started. On validation of the log on it establishes the operating environment for the specific user. In conjunction with this the Server also provides the User Preferences dialog.
\par \pard 
\par The server maintains a window for the display of messages and a log file.
\par 
\par On request, or when all registered interface applications have closed, the server performs the log off function..
\par 
\par If you explicitly attempt to close the Server it will request permission from all the currently registered interface applications. Only if all applications grant permission will the server close, it may therefore be necessary to close all interface applications before closing the server.
\par \pard 
