\pard\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Suppress Warnings
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 This \ul User Preferences\plain\fs24 {\v User_Preferences} setting affects the action when a \ul warning\plain\fs24 {\v Warning_messages} message occurs
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Action If Set
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 The message is displayed in the \ul message Window\plain\fs24 {\v Message_Window}
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b Action if not set
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 The message is not displayed in the message window.
\par \pard\tx355 Note that it is still inserted into the list of \ul unacknowledged messages\plain\fs24 {\v Unacknowledged_messages} and is overridden by the \ul acknowledge on event\plain\fs24 {\v Acknowledge_on_event} user preference.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Unacknowledged messages}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Unacknowledged_messages}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} small}
\pard\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Unacknowledged messages
\par \plain\fs24 If Error or Warning messages are not \ul acknowledged when they occur\plain\fs24 {\v Acknowledge_on_event} they are inserted into a list of unacknowledged messages.
\par 
\par While there are unacknowledged messages the \ul message window\plain\fs24 {\v Message_Window} caption displays
\par [E]\tab Unacknowledged errors
\par [W]\tab Unacknowledged warnings
\par [E+W]\tab Unacknowledged errors and warnings
\par 
\par These messages may be reviewed by selecting the \ul Review Unacknowledged Messages\plain\fs24 {\v Review_Unacknowledged_Messages} entry in  the system menu of the Message Window
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \page
