\pard\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 User Access Level
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 All parameters and commands are assigned a \ul category\plain\fs24 {\v GEE4AL@admin32.hlp}
\par \pard\tx355 The User Access level is defines which parameters are displayed for selection purposes (e.g. in the status window selection, annotation parameter selection etc)
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The levels of choice permitted are defined by the Administrator in the \ul user profile\plain\fs24 {\v V_JNBJ@admin32.hlp}
\par \pard\tx355 \b Some SEM Control panels are restricted by access level.\fs28 
\par \pard\tx355 Novice Mode: 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\f5\fs24 Displays only those items assigned as Novice category
\par \pard\tx355 \f1 
\par \pard\tx355 \b\fs28 Expert Mode:\f5 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 Displays items assigned as Novice and Expert Category.
\par \pard\tx355 \f5 
\par \pard\tx355 \f1\b\fs28 Service Mode:\f5\fs24 
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\f5\fs24 Displays all items
\par \page
