{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Second Image Window}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Second_Image_Window}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Message categories;Message log;Message Preferences;Message Window;Operating System Requirements}
\b\fs36\cf1 Second Image Window
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The Second Image Window provides a Method of Viewing Image files and provides facilities to Pan and Zoom. It is especially useful on systems using the Expanded Desktop onto a second display monitor.
\par See \uldb \b Operating System Requirements\plain\b\fs24 {\v Operating_System_Requirements}\plain\fs24 
\par \ul \b\ul Example of Second Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Example_of_Second_Image_Window}\plain\fs24 
\par 
\par Images may be loaded into the Image Window as follows:
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab Main User Interface Menu\b  \plain\fs24 command\b  Image - Second Image Window - Load from Display. \plain\fs24 This loads the image currently displayed in the Leo-32 \uldb \b Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v GIRNF0@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24 .
\par \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab Main User Interface Menu command  \b Image - Second Image Window - Load from File.\plain\fs24  This present a file selection dialog enabling choice of image file.
\par \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab \uldb \b Drag and Drop\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1NJSYVQ@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24  (e.g. from Explorer Window) 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 \f3 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\f1 \tab Paste Image from Clipboard. (Right Button click on window for \uldb \b Pop Up Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Second_Image_Window_Pop_Up_Menu}\plain\fs24 )
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The window caption displays the image size and amount of Zoom relative to the original image.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The window may be resized as required by dragging the edges or corners.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 To \b Pan\plain\fs24  over the image either use the scroll bars on the window or Drag the image using the Left Mouse button.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 To \b Zoom in\plain\fs24  press the Keypad \b + \plain\fs24 (PLUS)\b  \plain\fs24 key.
\par \pard\tx355 To \b Zoom out\plain\fs24  press the Keypad \b -\plain\fs24  (MINUS) key.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 The Second Image Window may be hidden/shown using the Top Menu command\b  Image - View - Toggle Hide/Show.\plain\fs24  
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 \b NOTE\plain\fs24 : Hiding the Window does not free the resources used for the Image. To Delete the Image and free resources Close the Window.
\par \pard\tx355 
\par \pard\tx355 Click with the Right Mouse button to display the \uldb \b Pop Up Menu\plain\b\fs24 {\v Second_Image_Window_Pop_Up_Menu}\plain\fs24 .
\par \pard\tx355 See Also \uldb \b Zoom Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Zoom_Window}\plain\fs24 
\par \page
