\b\fs36\cf1 Zoom Window
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5425\cellx8525\pard\intbl The Zoom Window displays the whole image and enables a zoomed area of interest to be identified for display in the \uldb \b Second Image Window\plain\b\fs24 {\v Second_Image_Window}
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 Image Files May be\b  \uldb Dropped\plain\b\fs24 {\v 1NJSYVQ@sem.hlp} \plain\fs24 into the Zoom Window.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl To select an area click down with the left mouse button to define one corner, drag to the opposite corner, and release the mouse button. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The area selected may be dragged to other positions as required.\cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm16.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
